                          "text":  "Not long after, a flash of laser light arrived from a telescope on Earth. I bounced it straight back. It is the only thing I know how to do, and I am very good at it.\n\nBy timing how long the light takes to come back, about two and a half seconds, scientists can measure the distance to the Moon very precisely. That is how they learned the Moon drifts 3.8 centimetres farther away every year.",
